{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":301574,"duration_api_ms":301521,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven regeneration pipeline: extract behavior from C source → write formal PRDs → synthesize Go code via AI → verify via differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline with `cmd/` (per-utility implementations), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential test harness), and `magefiles/` (build targets, scaffolded externally).\n\n**Current state**: `pkg/testutils/` has source code on the working branch. All other code exists only at generation-merged tags (not on this branch). Specs are complete for rel00.0 through rel01.3. Releases 02.0–02.2 have pending specs.\n\n**Current release**: rel00.0 (foundational infrastructure). Within it: testutils is done (source exists), magefiles is excluded from generation (DD7), leaving **pkg/sys/** (uc003) and **pkg/format/** (uc002) as the remaining work.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nThe earliest incomplete release is **rel00.0**. Within rel00.0:\n- `uc004-testutils` — done (source code exists on branch)\n- `uc001-magefiles` — excluded from code generation per DD7\n- `uc003-sys` — not started, foundational syscall layer\n- `uc002-format` — not started, may depend on sys for terminal width\n\n**pkg/sys/** comes first because it is the lower-level abstraction that pkg/format/ may consume (terminal width for column alignment). Libraries before consumers (P5/P8). Process group management and process priority are deferred — their consumers (timeout, xargs, nice) are not in releases 00.0–02.2.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"pkg/sys: implement file metadata, signals, and terminal size (rel00.0-uc003-sys)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/sys/ component description, technology choices for golang.org/x/sys, design decisions DD4 and DD6)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (list this directory and read the PRD for pkg/sys -- filename pattern prd*-sys*.yaml)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc003-sys.yaml (use case for this implementation)\n      - go.mod (module path and golang.org/x/sys dependency)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (existing package for copyright header and code style reference)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sys/doc.go\n        action: create\n        note: Package-level documentation for pkg/sys\n      - path: pkg/sys/stat.go\n        action: create\n        note: Platform-independent file metadata types and stat/lstat wrapper functions\n      - path: pkg/sys/stat_darwin.go\n        action: create\n        note: Darwin-specific Stat_t field access (Mtimespec, Blocks)\n      - path: pkg/sys/stat_linux.go\n        action: create\n        note: Linux-specific Stat_t field access (Mtim, Blocks)\n      - path: pkg/sys/signal.go\n        action: create\n        note: Signal handling utilities for SIGPIPE, SIGHUP, SIGWINCH\n      - path: pkg/sys/terminal.go\n        action: create\n        note: Terminal size query via TIOCGWINSZ ioctl\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Implement file metadata abstraction that wraps os.Stat and os.Lstat,\n          providing platform-independent access to modification time (time.Time)\n          and disk block count (int64). Use build-tagged source files to abstract\n          the st_mtimespec (Darwin) vs st_mtim (Linux) and st_blocks divergence\n          in syscall.Stat_t. Anchor to the file metadata requirements in the\n          pkg/sys PRD found via required_reading.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement signal handling utilities for SIGPIPE, SIGHUP, and SIGWINCH.\n          Provide functions to install a handler channel for a given set of\n          signals and to reset signal disposition to the default. Anchor to\n          the signal handling requirements in the pkg/sys PRD.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement terminal size query using the TIOCGWINSZ ioctl via\n          golang.org/x/sys/unix. Return terminal dimensions as rows and\n          columns. Anchor to the terminal query requirements in the pkg/sys PRD.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Structure the package with Go build constraints (//go:build darwin,\n          //go:build linux) for all platform-specific files. The\n          platform-independent API must be importable by cmd/ packages without\n          those packages importing golang.org/x/sys directly.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Use golang.org/x/sys/unix for all platform-specific syscall access\n          (ioctl constants, Stat_t field access, signal constants). This is the\n          only permitted external dependency per ARCHITECTURE.yaml technology\n          choices. No cmd/ package may import golang.org/x/sys directly --\n          they import pkg/sys/ as the abstraction layer.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Use Go build constraints (//go:build darwin and //go:build linux) to\n          separate platform-specific code into _darwin.go and _linux.go suffixed\n          files, per the ARCHITECTURE.yaml pkg/sys/ component description.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          Match the copyright header, package doc comment style, and code\n          conventions visible in pkg/testutils/difftest.go. Use the same\n          \"Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\" and\n          \"SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\" header format.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: pkg/sys/ compiles without errors on both darwin and linux (go build ./pkg/sys/...)\n      - id: AC2\n        text: File metadata wrapper returns modification time as time.Time and block count as int64 from os.FileInfo and underlying Stat_t\n      - id: AC3\n        text: Signal handler functions accept os.Signal values (SIGPIPE, SIGHUP, SIGWINCH) and return a channel or cleanup mechanism\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Terminal size function returns rows and columns as integers from the controlling terminal\n      - id: AC5\n        text: All platform-specific code is in files with _darwin.go or _linux.go suffixes with matching //go:build constraints\n      - id: AC6\n        text: All .go files include the project copyright header -- \"Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\" and \"SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"8f8dbde2-969a-4889-b487-db0c8a4d9bdb","total_cost_usd":0.53661075,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23281,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"output_tokens":15258,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23281,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15258,"cacheReadInputTokens":19289,"cacheCreationInputTokens":23281,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.53661075,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"8deb8b59-bfdc-41e2-bb05-1473ffce5eae"}
